# sync-skills replicate list (example)
#
# Copy this file to `sync-skills.replicate` (same directory) and list skills that
# ANOTHER tool installs into the Claude Code user scope (~/.claude/skills/<name>)
# and that you want devkit to fan OUT to the other AI environments (Codex, Cursor).
#
# devkit does NOT own or import these skills — the owning tool installs and updates
# them. /sync-skills only symlinks ~/.codex/skills/<name> and
# ~/.cursor/skills/<name> to the owner copy at ~/.claude/skills/<name>, so a skill
# the owner ships once is reachable from every agent. Listing a skill here also
# stops /sync-skills from flagging it as "installed but not present in devkit".
#
# If the owner copy isn't installed, the entry is inert — nothing happens. An empty
# or absent list is a complete no-op: devkit has zero dependency on any owning tool.
#
# `sync-skills.replicate` is gitignored — your entries stay local and never reach
# this public repo. Only this .example file is committed.
#
# Caveat: replicated skills get the symlink only, not a generated Codex
# agents/openai.yaml (that's generated for devkit-owned skills). Codex still loads
# the skill; it just lacks the generated `interface:` metadata.
#
# Format: one bare skill name per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored;
# a `#` after an entry starts a trailing comment (stripped).
#
# Example (the cbc binary installs these into ~/.claude/skills):
# cbc
# cbc-orchestrator
# cbc-report
# cbc-peer
# cbc-recap
